{
  "_about": "Per lian-li-linux DeviceFamily facts (portability plan §4). LCD families: kind lcd, the screen role detect gives them (fan|pump|main|aux), the media aspect class, the media size a theme should ship, and the default orientation that turns that media onto the panel (compile adds the profile's role mount). LED families: kind (fan_group|strimer|ring|pump|duplicate|other), the calibration class, and for rings which role they light (pump|main). label is detect's default role label (ring_label for the ring of an AIO whose LCD has the label). Keys starting with _ are notes.",
  "_prep_defaults": {"fps": 30, "max_s": 120, "crf": 21, "maxrate": "8M", "image": "auto", "_about": "How lumenaire media prepare makes media for an LCD model (lib/pc-lights/media.sh, docs/MEDIA.md): prep.fps caps the frame rate (the daemon plays at most its default_fps, 30), max_s is the longest clip it keeps (longer sources use the first max_s seconds; models with transcode_cap_mb also get a size estimate), crf and maxrate drive libx264, image is the still format (auto: PNG for PNG/GIF/BMP or transparent sources, JPEG otherwise; png: always PNG). A model without prep uses these values. lconnect lists the L-Connect library folders made for the model (the media picker groups and ranks by them). compile reads neither key."},
